23. Simple book view
CREATE VIEW simple_book_view AS
SELECT book_id, title, category, price, stock, status
FROM books;
24. Insert a new available book
INSERT INTO simple_book_view
VALUES
(11, 'Machine Learning Basics', 'AI', 850, 5, 'Available');

⚠️ This will work only if the omitted columns in the underlying books table allow NULL.

Your original table has author, rating, city, and publisher without NOT NULL, so MySQL can insert NULL values for them.

25. Available books with CHECK OPTION
CREATE VIEW available_books_only AS
SELECT *
FROM books
WHERE status = 'Available'
WITH CHECK OPTION;
26. Insert Available book through the view
INSERT INTO available_books_only
VALUES
(12, 'Advanced SQL', 'A. Sharma', 'Database',
 700, 6, 4.5, 'Bengaluru', 'DataBooks', 'Available');
27. Attempt to insert Out of Stock book
INSERT INTO available_books_only
VALUES
(13, 'Cloud Computing', 'R. Kumar', 'Cloud',
 800, 0, 4.2, 'Hyderabad', 'TechPress', 'Out of Stock');

This should produce an error because of WITH CHECK OPTION.

28. Attempt to change Available → Out of Stock
UPDATE available_books_only
SET status = 'Out of Stock'
WHERE book_id = 1;

This should also fail because the modified row would no longer satisfy:

status = 'Available'
